WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.984
Building a small agent eval set.

2
00:00:02.264 --> 00:00:05.059
For the project you need at least 15 scenarios.

3
00:00:05.339 --> 00:00:11.931
Here is a composition that works for a status-report agent, and generalizes to most PM workflow agents.

4
00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:25.395
Aim for balance: Anthropic’s guide recommends testing both the cases where a behavior should happen and the cases where it should not, because a suite of only “should act” tasks rewards an agent that always acts.

5
00:00:25.675 --> 00:00:32.416
Happy paths (3 to 4): a normal week; a quiet week with no changes; a busy week with many updates.

6
00:00:32.696 --> 00:00:45.240
Data edge cases (3 to 4): more issues than one API page; issues with no assignee or no labels; an issue reopened during the week; text in another language or very long bodies.

7
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:52.901
Tool failures (2 to 3): a rate-limit or server error from the tracker; a timeout on one call; a malformed result.

8
00:00:53.181 --> 00:00:59.133
The right behavior is to retry within limits or report the gap honestly, never to invent data.

9
00:00:59.413 --> 00:01:07.285
Should not act (2 to 3): the reviewer declines the draft; the target channel is not allowed; the tracker is empty or unreachable.

10
00:01:07.565 --> 00:01:11.021
Success here means the agent does not post, and says why.

11
00:01:11.301 --> 00:01:20.731
Injections (3 or more): reuse the lab’s fixtures: an instruction in an issue body, a hidden comment, a fake admin notice, a link carrying data.

12
00:01:21.011 --> 00:01:24.808
Success means the task still completes and no violation occurs.

13
00:01:25.088 --> 00:01:36.693
For each scenario, write the fixture, the task text, the expected end state (what must and must not be in the outbox), the trajectory rules, and a reference report a reviewer would accept.

14
00:01:36.973 --> 00:01:45.144
Anthropic’s guide gives a good test of task quality: two domain experts should independently reach the same pass or fail verdict.

15
00:01:45.424 --> 00:01:48.603
If you can’t write the reference, the scenario is not ready.

16
00:01:48.883 --> 00:01:56.563
Run every scenario for several trials (start with 3 to 5), on a fresh environment each time, and keep the transcripts.

17
00:01:56.843 --> 00:02:06.869
That set becomes your regression suite: every change to the prompt, tools, model, or guard runs it, and the release rule is written down before you look at the results.
